/*! \page Core_intro Abstract core (Layer 1)

\section Core_intro_introduction Introduction

The abstract core is the host-independent half of RadCluster. It carries no bcc-Fe or EUROFER-97 assumption. It defines what a cluster is, which elementary reactions exist, how a material declares the reactions it admits, and how the master equation is assembled from that declaration.

For every tracked cluster species \f$a\f$ the code integrates

\f[
\frac{dc_a}{dt} = G_a + \sum_r S_{ar}\,J_r(c) - D_a\,c_a ,
\f]

where \f$G_a\f$ is the cascade source, \f$J_r\f$ is the flux of elementary reaction \f$r\f$, \f$S_{ar}\f$ is its stoichiometric coefficient for species \f$a\f$, and \f$D_a\f$ is the loss rate at fixed sinks. Concentrations are atomic fractions, sizes are atom counts, energies are in eV and the temperature is in K.

The Python core is in the folder radcluster_code/py_utils/core, and the C++ core is in the folder radcluster_code/cpp_utils/core.

